<h2 id="cookies">1. Cookies</h2>
<p>
  <strong>This site sets no cookies of its own, and no third party sets cookies through it.</strong> There is no
  advertising, no tag manager, no social tracking pixel, no Google Analytics, and no embedded video player.
</p>
<p>
  That is about web pages. Mail is different: the messages the application sends about an account carry tracking
  images put there by the mail provider, and
  <a href="/privacy/#account-mail">section 3.4 of the Privacy Policy</a> says what they do and how to keep them from
  loading.
</p>

<h2 id="storage">2. What is stored in your browser</h2>
<p>
  Three things may be written to your browser's local storage. None is a cookie, none is sent to a server
  automatically, and none is used to track you across sites. The visitor number in
  <a href="#choice">section 3</a> is not on this list: it is computed on my server each time a page view is counted,
  and nothing about it is written to your browser.
</p>

