<h2 id="control">5. How to block them</h2>
<p>
  Any content-blocking extension, or a browser in strict tracking-protection mode, will stop these requests. The site is
  built to stay readable without them: text, layout, navigation, the typeface and every icon are served entirely from
  this domain, and the GitHub activity graph is built into the page rather than fetched by your browser. On most pages
  there is nothing left to block. What you lose is the rendered GitHub statistics images on the
  <a href="/code/">Code</a> page. Such a blocker may also stop the page-view counter, which is fine: it is the
  same outcome as declining.
</p>
